{
  "format": "phaenon.json's \"roots\" and \"committed\" as its two readers answer them, the compiler (cmd/phn/project.go) and the Composer plugin (composer/src/ProjectFile.php; ../design/tooling.md §3.7): \"file\" is the project file's text. \"refused\" marks a file that is in error. Otherwise \"roots\" maps each source root to its output directory and \"committed\" lists the roots whose outputs the project commits, in the file's order, all as cleaned paths with forward slashes. \"compiler\" is part of the error of a file the compiler refuses for something other than the two keys, which the plugin, reading the two keys alone, answers as given.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "no key: the project commits no outputs (D13)",
      "file": "{\"roots\": {\"src\": \".src\", \"tests\": \".tests\"}}",
      "roots": {
        "src": ".src",
        "tests": ".tests"
      },
      "committed": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty list is no key",
      "file": "{\"roots\": {\"src\": \".src\"}, \"committed\": []}",
      "roots": {
        "src": ".src"
      },
      "committed": []
    },
    {
      "name": "null is no key",
      "file": "{\"roots\": {\"src\": \".src\"}, \"committed\": null}",
      "roots": {
        "src": ".src"
      },
      "committed": []
    },
    {
      "name": "one root of two: a library commits what its consumers load, not its tests",
      "file": "{\"roots\": {\"src\": \".src\", \"tests\": \".tests\"}, \"committed\": [\"src\"]}",
      "roots": {
        "src": ".src",
        "tests": ".tests"
      },
      "committed": [
        "src"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "every root",
      "file": "{\"roots\": {\"src\": \".src\", \"lib\": \".lib\"}, \"committed\": [\"src\", \"lib\"]}",
